# Left unset -- the Python backend at salesos-new.onrender.com currently
# returns 500 on real routes (confirmed via /telegram/link), and this value
# isn't set on the server, so it was only ever coming from this committed file.
# apiFetch() in src/lib/api.ts falls back to same-origin (this app's own
# TypeScript backend) when this is empty -- that's the working path every
# apiFetch-based feature (Telegram linking, AI assistant chat, audio
# analysis, employee/org admin actions, etc.) needs until the Python
# backend is actually deployed and verified working.
VITE_API_BASE_URL=""
